
#  LinkedList
   Step 1
   Think of it like a train

   [Data|Next] → [Data|Next] → [Data|Next] → null
      Node 1         Node 2         Node 3

   - Each Node has 2 things: data + pointer to next node
   - Head is just the reference to the first node
   - Last node points to null (end of list)

   Step 2
   Build the Node Class

   // A Node is just a box with 2 things inside
   class Node {
       int data;    // the value
       Node next;   // pointer to next node

       // constructor
       Node(int data) {
           this.data = data;
           this.next = null; // by default points to nothing
       }
   }

   Step 3
   Build the LinkedList Class (just head)

   class LinkedList {
       Node head; // just stores reference to first node

       // constructor - empty list
       LinkedList() {
           head = null;
       }
   }

   Visualize:
   Empty list:   head → null

   After adding 10:  head → [10|null]

   After adding 20:  head → [10|next] → [20|null]

   After adding 30:  head → [10|next] → [20|next] → [30|null]

   Step 4
   Insert at End (Append)

   void insertAtEnd(int data) {
       Node newNode = new Node(data); // create new node

       // Case 1: list is empty
       if (head == null) {
           head = newNode;
           return;
       }

       // Case 2: traverse to last node
       Node current = head;
       while (current.next != null) { // keep going until last
           current = current.next;
       }

       current.next = newNode; // attach new node at end
   }

   Visualize:
   insertAtEnd(10): head → [10|null]

   insertAtEnd(20):
     current starts at [10]
     current.next is null → stop
     attach 20 → head → [10|next] → [20|null]

   insertAtEnd(30):
     current starts at [10]
     current.next = [20] → move
     current.next = null → stop
     attach 30 → head → [10] → [20] → [30|null]

   Step 5
   Insert at Beginning (Prepend)

   void insertAtBeginning(int data) {
       Node newNode = new Node(data);

       // new node points to current head
       newNode.next = head;

       // head now points to new node
       head = newNode;
   }
   Visualize:
   Before: head → [10] → [20] → [30|null]

   insertAtBeginning(5):
     newNode = [5]
     newNode.next = head ([10])
     head = newNode

   After: head → [5] → [10] → [20] → [30|null]

   Step 6
   Insert at Position

   void insertAtPosition(int data, int position) {
       Node newNode = new Node(data);

       // position 0 = insert at beginning
       if (position == 0) {
           newNode.next = head;
           head = newNode;
           return;
       }

       // traverse to (position-1)th node
       Node current = head;
       for (int i = 0; i < position - 1; i++) {
           if (current == null) {
               System.out.println("Position out of range!");
               return;
           }
           current = current.next;
       }

       // insert between current and current.next
       newNode.next = current.next;
       current.next = newNode;
   }

   Visualize:
   List:  head → [10] → [20] → [30|null]
   insertAtPosition(99, 2)

   Traverse to position 1 → current = [20]
   newNode.next = current.next ([30])
   current.next = newNode

   After: head → [10] → [20] → [99] → [30|null]

   Step 7
   Delete by Value

   void delete(int data) {
       // Case 1: empty list
       if (head == null) {
           System.out.println("List is empty!");
           return;
       }

       // Case 2: delete head node
       if (head.data == data) {
           head = head.next; // just move head forward
           return;
       }

       // Case 3: find node before the one to delete
       Node current = head;
       while (current.next != null) {
           if (current.next.data == data) {
               current.next = current.next.next; // skip deleted node
               return;
           }
           current = current.next;
       }

       System.out.println("Value not found!");
   }

   Visualize:
   List: head → [10] → [20] → [30] → [40|null]
   delete(30)

   current = [10], current.next.data = 20 → move
   current = [20], current.next.data = 30 → FOUND!
   current.next = current.next.next ([40])

   After: head → [10] → [20] → [40|null]
            [30] is now disconnected → garbage collected ✅

   Step 8
   Print / Display the List

   void display() {
       if (head == null) {
           System.out.println("List is empty!");
           return;
       }

       Node current = head;
       while (current != null) {
           System.out.print(current.data);
           if (current.next != null) System.out.print(" → ");
           current = current.next;
       }
       System.out.println(" → null");
   }

   Step 9
   Reverse a LinkedList (Most Asked!)
   void reverse() {
       Node prev = null;
       Node current = head;
       Node next = null;

       while (current != null) {
           next = current.next;  // save next
           current.next = prev;  // reverse pointer
           prev = current;       // move prev forward
           current = next;       // move current forward
       }

       head = prev; // prev is now the new head
   }
   Visualize:
   Before: head → [10] → [20] → [30] → null

   Step 1: prev=null, current=[10], next=[20]
           [10].next = null
           prev=[10], current=[20]

   Step 2: prev=[10], current=[20], next=[30]
           [20].next = [10]
           prev=[20], current=[30]

   Step 3: prev=[20], current=[30], next=null
           [30].next = [20]
           prev=[30], current=null

   head = prev = [30]
   After: head → [30] → [20] → [10] → null ✅

   Step 10
   Search a Value
   boolean search(int data) {
       Node current = head;
       while (current != null) {
           if (current.data == data) return true;
           current = current.next;
       }
       return false;
   }

   Complexity Summary
   Operation	              Time	Space
   Insert at beginning	      O(1)	O(1)
   Insert at end	          O(n)	O(1)
   Insert at position	      O(n)	O(1)
   Delete	                  O(n)	O(1)
   Search	                  O(n)	O(1)
   Reverse	                  O(n)	O(1)